MILESTONE: every Phase 0 Red baseline spec now passes. The defect that opened
this track - role="slider" declared on all adapters with no keyboard handler
anywhere in packages/ - is closed across React, Vue and Svelte.

Delivered:
  - role=slider normalised onto the container in all three adapters; the handle
    is now role="presentation"
  - full ARIA: tabindex, aria-valuetext, aria-orientation, aria-keyshortcuts,
    aria-describedby, plus aria-disabled for Vue which lacked it
  - polite atomic live regions, accessibleFallback stepped/custom
  - stepping primitives on all three hooks/composables
  - visible focus indicator closing WCAG 2.2 SC 2.4.7
  - 64 new adapter specs

Design decision: the key map lives in @heelslide/core as resolveKeyAction, so
parity is structural. Three adapters cannot drift on what a key does, and the
deliberate omission of End is enforced once rather than three times.

Parity audited empirically, not assumed: 21 accessibility features checked
across all three adapters, all present. Two asymmetries found and fixed -
aria-hidden (resolved downward, since the handle subtree carries author
children) and AccessibleFallbackMode missing from React and Vue exports.

Noted for a future track: Svelte wildcards its type exports while React and Vue
enumerate, so the next new type will ship from one adapter and not the others
unless someone remembers. Not changed here - converting the other two would
widen their public surface beyond this track's remit.

useHeelslide.ts sits at exactly 80.00% branch coverage, on the gate rather than
comfortably above it.

